From 5d4dd96a5dc9e33180337116f3e0cff960cc941a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jackson NSANZIMANA <worldbesthighlights@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:37:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(css): only merge duplicate conditional group at-rules

merge-duplicate-at-rules keys every at-rule by `name + params`. That
identifies a block only for conditional group rules (@media, @supports,
@container). For anything else it is wrong:

- every @font-face has empty params, so all faces in one stylesheet
  collapse into a single rule; its repeated descriptors resolve last-wins,
  so only the last font face survives
- same-named @keyframes bodies are concatenated
- statement at-rules (@import url(a.css); @layer a, b;) are moved to the
  end of the stylesheet as empty blocks

@compiled/vite-plugin runs sort() on every CSS asset containing an atomic
class, which includes global stylesheets bundled next to .compiled.css
imports, so a design system's @font-face declarations are hit in practice.
sortAtRules: false does not help, because the merge runs regardless.

Only @media, @supports and @container are merged now; all other at-rules
are left where they are.
